oduction and design facts. Match the exact aircraft variant or named vessel; do not substitute a related model. Prefer substantive article pages over photo-gallery listings. Return only a compact JSON array of objects with title and exact_source_url. Use original source URLs, never invented URLs or AI encyclopedias. No prose or excerpts.","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"S1","source_tier":3,"source_tier_label":"Tier 3 reference/secondary","source_title":"USS S-1 (Submarine No. 105, later SS-105), 1920–1942 — Naval History and Heritage Command Photographic Archives","source_url":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","source_variant_selection":{"evaluated_variants":[{"covered_slot_count":3,"distinct_slot_excerpt_count":0,"excerpt_count":10,"method_priority":1,"source_capture_method":"fetched_page","text_chars":8799,"text_hash":"8b29afae47f12971f668edca3065dbaa5787315c155fc279a79c18a759dfae8e"}],"selected_capture_method":"fetched_page","selected_variant":{"covered_slot_count":3,"distinct_slot_excerpt_count":0,"excerpt_count":10,"method_priority":1,"source_capture_method":"fetched_page","text_chars":8799,"text_hash":"8b29afae47f12971f668edca3065dbaa5787315c155fc279a79c18a759dfae8e"},"selection_rule":"highest Anton-slot coverage, then distinct required-slot excerpts, then excerpt count; fetched_page wins exact ties"},"text":"Online Image: 54KB; 740 x 305 pixels Photo #: NH 72793 USS S-1 (SS-105) With a Martin MS-1 scouting floatplane (Bureau # A-6525) on her after deck, probably at Norfolk, Virginia, on 24 October 1923.","text_hash":"b4260daee87961e24a2bdebcacc5db6bc46e1b8c3a7e76c492b910529d92306e"},{"excerpt_id":"DVSU1-E1","locator":"DVSU1-E1; R1-E1; source=https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","original_excerpt_id":"R1-E1","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"DVSU1","source_tier":3,"source_title":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","source_url":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","text":"USS S-1 (Submarine # 105, later SS-105), 1920-1942 USS S-1 , first of a numerous class of Electric Boat Company type 854-ton submarines, was built at Quincy, Massachusetts. Commissioned in June 1920, she mainly served in New England waters until 1922, when she was modified to both bring her up to current standards with a larger deck gun and to fit her for experimental use as a base for a small scouting seaplane. S-1 spent the next several years conducting tests with Martin MS-1 aircraft, then returned to regular operational use. During the later 1920s she made several deployments to the Caribbean area, and in 1930 was transferred to Pearl Harbor, Hawaii. S-1 was based in Hawaii for seven years, returning to the East Coast in July 1937 to be laid up. She decommissioned at the Philadelphia Navy Yard in October of that year and remained in reserve until recalled to active duty in October 1940, part of the Nation's response to the outbreak of World War II more than a year earlier. While operating in a training capacity in 1940-1941 S-1 made two trips to Bermuda. In April 1942 she was decommissioned and transferred to the United Kingdom.","text_hash":"53b4814fd1c8be334ae676da5f900bd40c7e7bed517e64cd4742afc66155afc6"},{"excerpt_id":"DVSU1-E2","locator":"DVSU1-E2; R1-E2; source=https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","original_excerpt_id":"R1-E2","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"DVSU1","source_tier":3,"source_title":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","source_url":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","text":"USN Ships--USS S-1 (Submarine # 105, later SS-105) Return to Naval History and Heritage Command home page. Return to Online Library listing","text_hash":"075f8698e41af6a346b65fd33350ae1995358b787fa040f9302b358994c981a9"},{"excerpt_id":"DVSU1-E3","locator":"DVSU1-E3; R1-E3; source=https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","original_excerpt_id":"R1-E3","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"DVSU1","source_tier":3,"source_title":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","source_url":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","text":"The images listed in this box are NOT in the Naval History and Heritage Command's collections. DO NOT try to obtain them using the procedures described in our page \"How to Obtain Photographic Reproductions\". For more images related to this submarine, see: USS S-1 (Submarine # 105, later SS-105) -- Part II . NOTES: To the best of our knowledge, the pictures referenced here are all in the Public Domain, and can therefore be freely downloaded and used for any purpose. Some images linked from this page may bear obsolete credit lines citing the organization name: \"Naval Historical Center\". Effective 1 December 2008 the name should be cited as: \"Naval History and Heritage Command\". If you want higher resolution reproductions than the digital images presented here, see: \"How to Obtain Photographic Reproductions.\" Return to Naval History and Heritage Command home page. Page made 27 November 2004 Coding updated 22 November 2010","text_hash":"381a41d5c3a8c344c67c8afdf40f849d6f747302950f6903b96bd1554921e5e1"},{"excerpt_id":"DVSU1-E4","locator":"DVSU1-E4; R1-E5; source=https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","original_excerpt_id":"R1-E5","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"DVSU1","source_tier":3,"source_title":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","source_url":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","text":"USS S-1 (Submarine # 105, later SS-105), 1920-1942 USS S-1 , first of a numerous class of Electric Boat Company type 854-ton submarines, was built at Quincy, Massachusetts.","text_hash":"b8d362a31a0ccaa5f11447f4895b26f0efcce08169641bbc514d8619d7b49f88"},{"excerpt_id":"DVSU1-E5","locator":"DVSU1-E5; R1-E6; source=https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","original_excerpt_id":"R1-E6","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"DVSU1","source_tier":3,"source_title":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","source_url":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","text":"Photo #: NH 104991 USS S-1 (Submarine # 105) Possibly photographed near the New London Submarine Base, Groton, Connecticut, circa 1919. S-1 was launched in late October 1918, but not commissioned until mid-1920, so it is possible that this photograph shows her during an early trial period, as she appears to not be fully outfitted.","text_hash":"ac22e84527d7248c33abf6ad5a4144eab99793bfce8fb3948d197bb94150de83"},{"excerpt_id":"DVSU1-E6","locator":"DVSU1-E6; R1-E9; source=https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","original_excerpt_id":"R1-E9","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"DVSU1","source_tier":3,"source_title":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","source_url":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","text":"Photo #: NH 104991 USS S-1 (Submarine # 105) Possibly photographed near the New London Submarine Base, Groton, Connecticut, circa 1919.","text_hash":"e912daa498bad8808da2370f73fc6f7e14da2ab6561ddc26b97e82b1b2437189"},{"excerpt_id":"DVSU1-E7","locator":"DVSU1-E7; R1-E10; source=https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-usn/usnsh-s/ss105.htm","original_excerpt_id":"R1-E10","source_capture_method":"fetched_page","source_id":"DVSU1","source_tier":3,"source_title":"https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/On